          "headline": "Rupee hits seven-month high near 92.3 per dollar on heavy foreign buying",
          "summary": "The rupee opened at 92.65 per dollar, up from Monday's 92.85, and strengthened to about 92.26 by 1:40 pm. Foreign investors bought a net ₹5,673 crore of Indian shares on Monday, and cheaper oil helped too. The dollar index was firmer at about 104 ahead of US inflation and GDP data at 7 pm IST.",
